/**
 * An asteroid belt flown left to right. Drift reads `#` as asteroid rock, `C` as ice, `~` as nebula
 * dust, `>` as solar wind, `o` as stardust, `?` as a supply pod, `*` as a space mine, `j` as a plasma
 * orb, `S` as a Rocket Ray, `E` as a Moon Worm and `K` as a Moon Mite. Rows 0-2 and 27-29 are solid.
 * `g` and `i` form the banded disc, `d` is metal shielding, and `a/l/r/p/q` form open wormway arches.
 *
 * - Cols 1-98, rows 17-26: the opening straight from the starts, to learn the drift.
 * - Cols 87-172: an S-bend up cols 87-98 into the top corridor (rows 3-12), round a planet at each
 *   inner corner (col 85 row 15, col 100 row 14); in the corridor a Rocket Ray, a Moon Worm in the
 *   ceiling, a plasma orb and a space mine, with asteroids to weave between.
 * - Cols 170-216: the ice gate, a wall of ice at cols 192-194 (rows 4-9) straight ahead; the longer
 *   way round drops below the island at cols 177-209 (rows 11-17) and back up.
 * - Cols 217-278: the dust field (cols 224-270, rows 5-23) with clean lanes at rows 3-4, 12-13, 18
 *   and 24-25.
 * - Cols 279-338: the solar wind lane (cols 284-330, rows 12-15), a Moon Worm above it and a Moon
 *   Mite on the floor below.
 * - Cols 339-602: THE GAS GIANT. A gentle gravity bend leads into a split around the banded planet
 *   (col 455 row 13). Take the wide upper dust belt or bank under the disc, between ice moonlets
 *   and the floor, into the solar wind at cols 481-504. The lanes rejoin and climb before the exit.
 * - Cols 603-846: THE DEBRIS STORM. A lone asteroid at col 643 teaches the crossing. Six sweeps
 *   at different heights and speeds, plasma orbs and rock shelves share the fast low road. Dust
 *   covers the final sweep at col 776. The high road climbs above the shield (cols 631-773), where
 *   staggered baffles and belts of dust cost time.
 * - Cols 847-926, dark: MOON SHADOW, a corridor in a moon's shadow (rows 3-14, wider at the entry)
 *   with a Rocket Ray, a Moon Worm and a plasma orb.
 * - Cols 927-1214: THE WORMWAYS. A two-way pair crosses the sealed wall at cols 966-970. In the
 *   chamber, cross the top or choose a shortcut beside a black hole (col 1083 row 20), a small
 *   warp across an alcove, or a one-way loop back to the chamber's start. A later mouth puts the
 *   racer inside a planet's reach (col 1153 row 21). One last pair leads into BLACK HOLE SPLIT.
 * - Cols 1215-1291: the late split round an island (cols 1223-1283, rows 10-20), dark through col 1226.
 *   The shortcut runs along rows 7-9 between black holes in pockets above (col 1248 row 4) and below
 *   (col 1263 row 12), inside both reaches. The main way drops down cols 1215-1222 round a planet
 *   at the island's top-left corner (col 1224 row 11), runs along rows 21-26 past a Moon Mite, and
 *   climbs cols 1284-1291 round a planet at its bottom-right corner (col 1282 row 19).
 * - Cols 1292-1373: the run home, entered above row 13, past an asteroid (cols 1316-1321) and a
 *   space mine. The finish is col 1372.
 *
 * Two asteroids cross the opening straight (cols 30 and 62) and three cross the dust field
 * (cols 238, 247, and 256). Their offsets and the Debris Storm's put neighbours out of step.
 */
